#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:1
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:850
#, no-wrap
msgid "Magic"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Magic is a potent ally but a dangerous adversary. All armies make use of "
"some sort of sorcery so it is important to have a grasp of the arcane "
"abilities that lie at your command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Only Wizards can cast spells. The term ‘Wizard’ includes various types of "
"sorcerer such as Orc Shamans, Elven Mages, Undead Liche Priests as well as "
"human Wizards.  Every army’s magic is different and some are better than "
"others as we shall see. Individual spells are listed in the "
"xref:revolution:armies:index.adoc[Army Lists]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:17
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Magic items"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Magic items are devices such as banners, swords or armour that confer "
"special attacks, protection, etc. Each magic item has its own rules and "
"points value. When you choose an army you can include magic items in it.  "
"Any unit of infantry, cavalry or chariots can be given one magic item. Each "
"character can also be given one magic item. If you decide to give a magic "
"item to a unit or character then you must pay the extra points. This means "
"that you will have fewer points for other troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Magic items cannot be given to monsters or war machines. Some items can only "
"be given to characters or to a Wizard as described later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Casting spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:45
msgid ""
"In his Shooting phase, each Wizard can cast one spell from the spell lists "
"for his army. He can cast a spell even if he has joined a unit that is "
"engaged in combat. The spell has a range just like a shooting weapon and the "
"target unit must lie within this distance. Unlike shooting from missile "
"weapons, the Wizard does not have to target the closest enemy unit but can "
"choose whichever enemy unit he wants. The Wizard is assumed to be able to "
"see all round though his vision will be blocked by unit stands and terrain "
"as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:49
msgid ""
"The Wizard nominates the target and must roll the required dice score to "
"make the spell work; usually 4+, 5+ or 6 depending on how difficult the "
"spell is to cast."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:55
msgid ""
"If you are successful, the spell works as described. If not then the spell "
"has failed and there is no effect. The score required is sometimes modified "
"but, regardless of any modifier, a dice roll of 1 always fails and a roll of "
"6 always succeeds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Wizards can cast spells against any eligible targets within range, but a "
"unit can only ever be affected by the same spell once in any turn. A unit "
"has been affected if a spell has worked by rolling the appropriate dice "
"score, has not been dispelled or antimagicked, and its effect has been "
"resolved on the unit as per the spell description.  Note that a spell might "
"take full effect but still cause no damage – a "
"xref:revolution:armies:empire.adoc#ball-of-flame[Ball of Flame] inflicts 3 "
"shooting attacks for example but all 3 might fail to score hits or hits "
"might be nullified by armour."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:76
msgid ""
"There are some situations where the target of a spell is not literally a "
"unit – for example the xref:revolution:armies:empire.adoc#ball-of-flame[Ball "
"of Flame] and xref:revolution:armies:orcs.adoc#gotcha[Gotcha] spells inflict "
"shooting attacks upon all units that lie within their path. In these cases, "
"all units are affected once the appropriate dice roll has been scored to "
"make the spell work and assuming it is not dispelled or antimagicked. Note "
"that this means a unit can potentially be struck by two different Ball of "
"Flame spells coming from different directions – but only the first will "
"affect it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Where there might be room for doubt, the spell descriptions specifically "
"remind players that spells cannot affect the same unit twice. This is just "
"to clarify the rule where it was felt worthwhile to do so. The rule applies "
"to all spells not just those that contain a separate note."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling e.g.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Logically minded players might quibble that a spell could be cast upon a "
"unit any number of times, blasting it to pieces with fireballs from dozens "
"of wizards.  The restriction exists so that magic is rarely enough to cause "
"casualties on its own. Magic is intended to augment conventional tactics and "
"weaponry but not form a battle-winning tactic in itself. For this reason "
"wizards are allowed to target their spells upon specific foes, selectively "
"augmenting conventional weaponry, but are prohibited from picking out single "
"units for annihilation with the same destructive spell cast over and over "
"again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:104
msgid ""
"Our armies rely on brute strength, courage and meticulous training to "
"overthrow their opponents... and if that doesn’t work there’s always "
"sorcery. It’s not just Wizards that get to use magic. Units can have magic "
"items and other characters can carry them too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:116
msgid ""
"Magic is part and parcel of the fantastic world our armies are fighting "
"over. To keep things fair, each item is allotted a points value, just like "
"the troops themselves, and some items can only be used by certain races or "
"types of warrior. There are three broad types of magic item: <<magic-"
"standards>> (most of which protect the unit carrying them in some way), "
"<<magic-weapons>> (which are carried by a unit’s leader and which usually "
"increase the unit’s fighting power) and <<devices-of-power>> (which increase "
"the leadership abilities of Generals, Wizards and Heroes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "Magic standards"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling available
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:133
msgid ""
"_A unit of infantry, cavalry or chariots can be given a single Magic "
"Standard. Characters and other types of units cannot be given Magic "
"Standards. An army can never include more than a single example of each type "
"of standard. Magic Standards serve to make a unit more difficult to destroy "
"by increasing its Armour value or number of Hits. The effect doesn’t apply "
"on any attached stands (such as Empire Skirmishers) or characters.  Some "
"banners have various ranks available only to units with specific values of "
"Armour or Hits._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:142
msgid ""
"As a general rule, a unit or character can only have one magic item. A unit "
"of infantry can have a Magic Banner or a Magic Weapon, for example, but not "
"both. Similarly, a Wizard can have a Magic Weapon or a Device of Power but "
"not one of each. Furthermore, a specific item may only appear in an army "
"once. You cannot have two Banners of Fortitude or three Swords of Cleaving, "
"for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:143
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Battle Banner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:146
msgid "[.cost]#Cost# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:153
msgid ""
"A unit with this banner increases the Attacks value of each of its stands by "
"+1 during its first Combat engagement of fighting.  The effect only lasts "
"for the first combat engagement of the battle, including rounds of pursuit "
"combat during the same engagement and any further engagements which result "
"from an advance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Banner of Shielding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:157
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – superior (units with Armour 4+ only)# [.points]#50 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:159
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – major (units with Armour 5+ only)# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:161
msgid ""
"[.cost]#Cost – minor (units with Armour 6+ or 0 only)# [.points]#15 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:169
msgid ""
"A unit with this banner has its Armour value increased in effectiveness by \\"
"+1. If the unit’s Armour value is 5+ then this banner increases it to 4+ and "
"so on. A unit’s Armour value cannot be better than 3+. If a unit already has "
"an Armour value of 3+ then this banner has no effect. This bonus lasts until "
"the unit loses a stand. After the unit has lost a stand, the banner has no "
"further effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Banner of Fortitude"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:173
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – major (units with 4 Hits only)# [.points]#50 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:175
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – minor (units with 3 or 2 Hits only)# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:184
msgid ""
"A unit with this banner increases the Hits value of each of its stands by +1 "
"during its first Combat engagement of fighting.  The effect only lasts for "
"the first combat engagement of the battle, including rounds of pursuit "
"combat during the same engagement and any further engagements which result "
"from an advance. Discard odd hits at the end of the Combat engagement before "
"discounting the effect of the Banner of Fortitude."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:185
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Banner of Steadfastness"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:188
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – superior (units with 4+ Armour only)# [.points]#20 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:190
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – major (units with 5+ Armour only)# [.points]#15 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:192
msgid "[.cost]#Cost – minor (units with 6+ Armour only)# [.points]#10 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:199
msgid ""
"One shooting hit inflicted on the unit after saves have been taken in each "
"turn is ignored because the missiles are cast aside by the Banner of "
"Steadfastness. This includes hits from magic spells inflicted in the "
"Shooting phase. This effect lasts until the unit loses a stand. After the "
"unit has lost a stand the banner has no further effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Banner of Fortune"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:203
msgid "[.cost]#Cost# [.points]#15 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:213
msgid ""
"The player can choose to immediately re-roll all the unit’s Attack dice once "
"in either the Shooting phase or Combat phase. This includes any bonus "
"attacks from magic items or characters. The player declares that he is "
"unsatisfied with the scores he has rolled, takes all the dice and "
"immediately rolls them all once again. Note that the player must roll all "
"the dice again, including any that have scored hits, so it is possible to be "
"very unfortunate and roll an even worse score! The Banner of Fortune works "
"only once during the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Magic weapons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:221
msgid ""
"_Magic weapons can be carried by an infantry, cavalry or chariot unit or by "
"a character. Only a single example of each type of magic weapon can be "
"included in an army._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sword of Destruction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:225
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:245
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:252
msgid "[.cost]#Cost# [.points]#10 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:231
msgid ""
"If a unit has this weapon then one enemy unit that it is touching is "
"affected and must re-roll one successful Armour roll in each round of "
"combat. For example, if three hits are scored and one is saved by armour "
"then the successful roll must be taken again. Only one enemy unit can be "
"affected by this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sword of Fate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:235
msgid "[.cost]#Cost# [.points]#5 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:241
msgid ""
"In the first round of the unit’s first combat, a unit with this sword adds a "
"+1 bonus to the Attack value of one stand in a similar way as the Attack "
"bonus of a character. The Sword of Fate only works once in the entire game. "
"Note that this gives +1 Attack in total and not +1 to each stand!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:242
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sword of Cleaving"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:248
msgid ""
"A unit with this sword can re-roll one unsuccessful Attack dice each round "
"of combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sword of Might"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:256
msgid ""
"A unit with this sword adds a +1 bonus to the Attack value of one stand, "
"similar to the Attack bonus of a character. Note that this gives +1 Attack "
"in total, not +1 to each stand!"
msgstr ""

#.  Added to separate section
#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:260
#, no-wrap
msgid "Devices of power"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:264
msgid ""
"_Devices of power can be carried by characters. Only a single example of "
"each device can be included in an army._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crown of Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:268
msgid "[.cost]#General only# [.points]#70 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:275
msgid ""
"If the General has this potent magic item he can choose to issue his first "
"order of each turn against an unmodified Command value of 10. No command "
"penalties apply when the Crown of Command is used. This only applies to the "
"General’s first order each turn, subsequent orders must be given normally. "
"Should the General fail to issue his first order, by rolling an 11 or 12, "
"then the Crown of Command ceases to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helm of Dominion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:279
msgid "[.cost]#General only# [.points]#40 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:285
msgid ""
"Only a General is allowed to wear the Helm of Dominion (only his head is big "
"enough!). The General’s Command value is increased by +1 up to a maximum "
"value of 10. The Helm of Dominion works for one turn only during the entire "
"battle, the player must specify at the start of the turn if he wishes to "
"employ its powers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:286
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orb of Majesty"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:289
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:320
msgid "[.cost]#General only# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:296
msgid ""
"If the General has this magic item he may disregard a single failed Command "
"test and roll it again as if he had a Command value of 8. The usual "
"adjustments are made for Command penalties but note that the previously "
"failed roll is disregarded so it doesn’t count as a penalty. If the re-roll "
"is successful the order is issued and the General can continue issuing "
"orders in the usual way with his normal Command value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:299
msgid ""
"The Orb of Majesty will only work once in the entire game and only affects "
"an order that has been issued by the General."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ring of Magic"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:303
msgid "[.cost]#Wizard only# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:306
msgid ""
"A Wizard with this ring is able to cast a spell without making the usual "
"dice roll to do so. This item will only work once in the entire game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:307
#, no-wrap
msgid "Staff of Spellbinding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:310
msgid "[.cost]#Wizard or Dwarf Runesmith only# [.points]#30 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:316
msgid ""
"If an enemy Wizard fails to cast a spell, he can be spellbound on the D6 "
"roll of a 4+. A spellbound Wizard suffers a −1 dice penalty each time he "
"tries to cast a spell. The Staff of Spellbinding ceases to work once it has "
"been used successfully. It follows that only one enemy Wizard can be "
"spellbound as a result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sceptre of Sovreignty"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:329
msgid ""
"If the General carries the Sceptre of Sovereignty, he may ignore one "
"blundered ‘double 6’ roll for an order made by either himself or any of the "
"army’s other characters. If the blunder is made by a subordinate character "
"you can roll to see what the blunder is before deciding whether to use the "
"Sceptre of Sovereignty or not. If ignored, the Command test is passed and "
"the character may continue issuing orders as normal. The steely will of the "
"Sceptre of Sovereignty reaches out and stays the incompetent wretch before "
"the deed is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:330
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scroll of Dispelling"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:333
msgid "[.cost]#Wizard or Dwarf runesmith only# [.points]#20 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:339
msgid ""
"If a Wizard or a Dwarf Runesmith has the Scroll of Dispelling he can "
"automatically cause an enemy’s spell to fail. The Scroll can only be used "
"once to nullify the effect of a spell an enemy Wizard has successfully cast. "
"In the case of a Runesmith, the Scroll can be used after a normal Dwarf anti-"
"magic roll has failed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wand of Power"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:343
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:352
msgid "[.cost]#Wizard only# [.points]#10 pts#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:348
msgid ""
"A Wizard with the Wand of Power can add +1 to the chance of a spell working "
"once during the game. The player must decide that he is using the Wand of "
"Power before rolling the dice. As always a spell fails on the roll of a 1 "
"even when using the Wand of Power."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rod of Repetition"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:363
msgid ""
"If a Wizard casts a spell and rolls sufficiently well for it to work then he "
"may cast another spell. He can only do this once during the entire game.  It "
"does not matter if the previous spell is dispelled or anti-magicked by a "
"Runesmith so long as the required dice score was rolled.  After any effects "
"of the previous spell have been resolved, the Wizard can decide to use the "
"Rod of Repetition to cast another spell – this can be the same spell again "
"or a different one. Note that the same spell can be cast upon the same unit "
"if the previous spell has been dispelled/anti-magicked.  This next spell is "
"cast exactly like any other – roll a dice to determine if it works in the "
"usual way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:374
msgid ""
"The xref:revolution:armies:empire.adoc#teleport[Teleport] spell already "
"allows the Wizard to cast a second, different spell.  The Rod of Repetition "
"may be used after the second spell has been successfully cast.  If it is "
"used to cast Teleport again then the bonus spell is lost.  This effectively "
"restricts casting to a maximum of 3 spells per turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:377
msgid "Assuming successful casting the possibilities are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:380
msgid ""
"Teleport → second spell → Rod of Repetition for a third spell (which could "
"be another Teleport), or"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/magic.adoc:381
msgid ""
"First spell (could be Teleport) → Rod of Repetition to cast Teleport → third "
"spell."
msgstr ""
